  "final_answer": "Based on my investigation of apple.com, I have the following findings:\n\n## Answer\n\n**The iPhone 14 Plus is no longer sold directly on apple.com.** Apple has discontinued this model and removed it from their main product lineup and online store. When attempting to access `apple.com/shop/buy-iphone/iphone14-plus`, the page returns a 404 \"Page Not Found\" error, and the device is not listed in the current iPhone lineup (which includes iPhone 18 Pro/Pro Max, iPhone Duo, iPhone Air, iPhone 17/Pro/Pro Max, iPhone 17e, iPhone 16/e/Plus, etc.).\n\nThe iPhone 14 Plus only appears on Apple's **Compare page** (https://www.apple.com/iphone/compare/), where it is marked with the label **\"Available at authorized resellers\"** instead of having a \"Buy\" button like the current models.\n\n### Key Information Found on apple.com:\n- **Colors available** (per Tech Specs at support.apple.com/en-us/111854): Midnight, Purple, Starlight, (PRODUCT)RED, Blue, Yellow ✅ Purple is one of the available colors\n- **Storage options**: 128GB, 256GB, 512GB ✅ 256GB is available\n- **Year introduced**: 2022\n\n### Original Launch Price (October 2022):\nWhen the iPhone 14 Plus was originally released by Apple:\n- 128GB: $899\n- **256GB: $999** ← This would have been the original price for the 256GB Purple model\n- 512GB: $1,099\n\n### Summary\nWhile the **iPhone 14 Plus in 256GB Purple was originally priced at $999 USD** at launch, this configuration **cannot currently be purchased new from apple.com** because Apple has discontinued the model. The only options for obtaining one would be through authorized resellers, third-party retailers, or Apple's Certified Refurbished store (where it also does not currently appear).",
